title: Chapter 12: Decision Architecture and Lifecycle Governance
---
flowchart TD
 S1["1. Open and maintain the lifecycle dossier\nRecord the problem, evidence, economics, governance, implementation, monitoring, changes, and decision status."]
 S2["2. Apply stage gates\nRequire proportionate evidence before procurement, silent validation, pilot, scale, or institutional dependence."]
 S1 --> S2
 S3["3. Implement through controlled validation\nVerify readiness, train users, validate locally, test fallback, and define acceptance criteria."]
 S2 --> S3
 S4["4. Operate algorithmovigilance\nReview technical, clinical, workflow, workforce, equity, economic, contractual, and trust indicators at defined intervals."]
 S3 --> S4
 S5["5. Investigate incidents and material changes\nPreserve data, versions, outputs, human actions, context, causes, corrective action, and revalidation."]
 S4 --> S5
 S6["6. Renew, restrict, replace, or de-adopt\nCompare current value, safeguards, alternatives, continuity, and exit readiness."]
 S5 --> S6
 S7["7. Feed lessons into portfolio governance\nUpdate policy, capability, procurement, training, standards, and strategic priorities."]
 S6 --> S7
